  throw std::runtime_error("boom");
} catch (const std::exception& e) {
  std::cerr << e.what() << '\n';
}
```

- **Remember:** Catch by `const` reference, not by value.
- **Common mistake:** Throwing raw pointers or catching by value (slicing).

